### Deploying EKS cluster
- it provides a way to deploy, manage and scale application containers
- pre-requisite is to create a IAM role with EKS policies attached to it
- For creating a cluster, we can make use of CloudFormation service available in AWS. It takes an existing template to create cluster with VPC attached to it.
- aws eks create-cluster --region us-east-1 --name EKSCluster1 --role-arn <eks-role-arn> --resource-vpc-config subnetIds=<subnet-1>,<subnet-2>,securityGroupIds=<sg-id>
- aws eks describe-cluster --region us-east-1 --name EKSCluster1 --query cluster.status 
- aws eks update-kubeconfig --region us-east-1 --name EKSCluster1 : It adds kube config to cluster so that it supports kubectl commands
- For creating a node in eks cluster, we nees to have an IAM role with required policies attached to it. Role must be created with use case as EC2 and AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy, AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly policies attached to it
- Under compute section of EKS cluster, create a node group with selected iam role and with no.of nodes.
